<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:Cortex">
<!--
    kuna `option cortexmpriv` (default-OFF opt-in, ON in the `aggressive` preset),
    P2 lift/inline-inject: the synthesized `isCurrentModePrivileged`
    `<callotherfixup>` registered in `infra/architecture.rs`
    (`register_cortexmpriv_fixup`) and consumed at
    `infra/decompile_drive.rs is_injected_userop`.

    ARMTHUMBinstructions.sinc models every VERSION_7M (Cortex-M) special-register
    move as a RUNTIME privilege test rather than as one operation:

        b:1 = isCurrentModePrivileged();
        if (!b) goto <notPriv>;
        <the real effect>
      <notPriv>

    Twelve constructors do it (mrs/msr against ipsr, primask, basepri,
    basepri_max, faultmask, control), so EVERY MRS/MSR costs one extra basic
    block and two extra CFG edges that exist in no source.  Upstream Ghidra has
    the same defect; IDA and Binary Ninja model MRS/MSR as a plain intrinsic.

    Witness (self-contained, 6 bytes at 0x1000, Thumb):

        f3ef 8011   mrs r0,basepri     ; the guarded constructor
        4770        bx  lr

    Pass 1 (default, cortexmpriv off): the bug - the read is wrapped in the
    privilege test, so a straight-line two-instruction function comes back with a
    branch and the user-op named in the emitted C.  Assertions #1 and #2.
    Pass 2 (option cortexmpriv on): the fix - the guard folds to the constant 1,
    its block and edges die, and the bare `getBasePriority()` read survives.
    Assertions #3 and #4.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000">
eff311807047
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="read_basepri"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>set context TMode 1 [ram,0x1000] [ram,0x1010]</com>
  <com>lo fu read_basepri</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option cortexmpriv on</com>
  <com>lo fu read_basepri</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CORTEXMPRIV #1: OFF leaves the privilege user-op in the emitted C (pass 1 only)" min="1" max="1">isCurrentModePrivileged\(\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CORTEXMPRIV #2: OFF turns a straight-line special-register read into a branch (pass 1 only)" min="1" max="1">^  if \(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CORTEXMPRIV #3: the real effect survives in BOTH passes" min="2" max="2">getBasePriority\(\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CORTEXMPRIV #4: ON folds the guard away, leaving one unconditional read (pass 2 only)" min="1" max="1">^  return getBasePriority\(\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
